# Laboratory inventory

Record planned and existing equipment, compute, locations, manual stations, and supporting systems.
An entry describes knowledge about an item. It does not authorize execution.

| Item | Stable ID | Type | Location | Evidence | Evidence state | Integration state | Twin state | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|

## State vocabulary

- Evidence: `planned`, `reported`, or `verified`.
- Integration: `not-started`, `simulated`, `integrated`, or `commissioned`.
- Visual twin: `none`, `planned`, `draft`, `registered`, or `validated`.

Keep the three states separate. A verified or modeled instrument can still lack an adapter. A
commissioned capability needs deployment-specific evidence outside this table.

